From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 20:57:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): selection positions are DIPs, not physical
 pixels

_mouseTo multiplied cell coordinates by _cellSize, which is in physical
pixels. libghostty applies the content scale to mouse positions itself, so
every selection landed scale-times too far across the screen - invisible at
100%, and roughly twice as far right as the pointer at 200%.

Measured rather than reasoned. Driving the same sequence through
harness/hwnd-host with GHOSTTY_HARNESS_SELECT asked for cells 2..4 and got
5..8 back, and asked for 5..9 and got 11..14; with a 19px cell on a 200%
display that is exactly one factor of the scale.

Worth noting how close this came to shipping as "selection feels off": it
would have been dismissed as imprecise dragging on the machine where it was
found, and been perfect on any 100% monitor a reviewer used.
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp      | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 2e73b270e..46a2155a0 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #include "pch.h"
 #include "GhosttyControlCore.h"
 #include "GhosttySettingsTranslator.h"
-#include "GhosttyKeyTranslator.h"
+#include "GhosttyKeyTranslator.h"
 #include "GhosttyCopyFormat.h"
 
 #include "GhosttyControlCore.g.cpp"
@@ -829,8 +829,19 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         {
             return;
         }
-        const auto x = (static_cast<double>(cell.X) + 0.5) * _cellSize.Width;
-        const auto y = (static_cast<double>(cell.Y) + 0.5) * _cellSize.Height;
+        // DIPs, not physical pixels. libghostty applies the content scale to
+        // mouse positions itself, and _cellSize is in pixels - so multiplying
+        // cells by it directly lands scale-times too far across the screen.
+        // On a 100% display that is invisible; at 200% a selection starts
+        // roughly twice as far right as the pointer.
+        //
+        // Measured, not reasoned: driving this sequence in harness/hwnd-host
+        // with GHOSTTY_HARNESS_SELECT on a 200% monitor asked for cells 2..4
+        // and got 5..8 back, and asked for 5..9 and got 11..14.
+        const auto cellWidth = _cellSize.Width / _compositionScale;
+        const auto cellHeight = _cellSize.Height / _compositionScale;
+        const auto x = (static_cast<double>(cell.X) + 0.5) * cellWidth;
+        const auto y = (static_cast<double>(cell.Y) + 0.5) * cellHeight;
         ghostty_surface_mouse_pos(_surface, x, y, GHOSTTY_MODS_NONE);
     }
 
